<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    isiZulu (Requirement 7).

    Translated for meaning rather than literally. isiZulu builds many of these ideas differently
    from English — "Mark taken" is rendered as an instruction to the reader rather than a label,
    and the noun-class agreement changes with the noun, so several strings could not simply reuse
    a stem.

    These need review by a first-language isiZulu speaker before submission. The developer is not
    one, and on a medication app an unchecked translation is a real risk rather than a cosmetic
    one. Where a term had no settled everyday equivalent — "biometric", "sync" — the widely
    understood English term has been kept rather than inventing one.
-->
